      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "4.3.1 IT and Technology Industry"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2g91svp",
      "content": "Hyderabad is the IT capital of Telangana and one of India's leading tech cities. HITEC City (Hyderabad Information Technology and Engineering Consultancy City) is the hub for major global IT companies."
    },
    {
      "id": "t6pgezs",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Major IT companies: Microsoft, Google, Amazon, Facebook, Apple, Wipro, Infosys, TCS, HCL",
        "Cyberabad – Largest IT cluster in India after Bengaluru",
        "T-Hub – India's largest startup incubator, located in Hyderabad",
        "Software exports from Telangana: Over $30 billion annually"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nb8vnab",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "4.3.2 Pharmaceuticals and Biotechnology"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1nerx2b",
      "content": "Telangana, particularly Hyderabad, is called the 'Genome Valley' and the 'Pharma Capital of India.' It contributes about 35% of India's total pharmaceutical exports."
    },
    {
      "id": "0s9iuku",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Genome Valley – World-class biotech cluster at Turkapally, Hyderabad",
        "Vaccine manufacturers: Bharat Biotech (Covaxin), Biological E, Serum Institute (Hyderabad unit)",
        "Major pharma companies: Dr. Reddy's Laboratories, Aurobindo Pharma, Hetero Drugs, Divi's Laboratories"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Distinguish clearly between Mission Kakatiya (irrigation/tank revival) and Mission Bhagiratha (piped drinking water).",
